message: "If you use this data set or code, please cite it as below, together with the accompanying paper."
title: "drone-ecology-forecast: bibliometric data and MATLAB growth-model pipeline for UAV research in ecology and environmental monitoring"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vedranu/drone-ecology-forecast"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22119199
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22119199
    description: "Zenodo archive of release v1.0-matlab"
authors:
  - given-names: "Vedran"
    family-names: "Uroš"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Organization and Informatics, University of Zagreb, Varaždin, Croatia"
  - given-names: "Marko"
    family-names: "Jelić"
    affiliation: "University of Applied Sciences “Marko Marulić” in Knin, Knin, Croatia"
keywords:
  - unmanned aerial vehicles
  - environmental monitoring
  - bibliometrics
  - technology forecasting
  - growth models
  - MATLAB
abstract: >-
  Annual OpenAlex counts (2005-2025) of articles combining UAV terms with ecological and
  environmental terms, with normalising denominators and six sub-domains, and a toolbox-free
  MATLAB pipeline fitting exponential, logistic, Gompertz and Bass growth models by Poisson
  deviance, comparing them with QAICc, backtesting them and producing negative-binomial
  bootstrap forecast intervals for 2028-2035.
